   },
   "note": "",
   "page": 8
  }
 ],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Counting",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Seven static toggle flip-flops form the counter. CP, through a Schmitt-trigger buffer, clocks the first; each of the others is clocked from the stage before it. The count advances on each HIGH-to-LOW transition of CP. Q0 to Q6 are the buffered outputs of stages 1 to 7."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Master reset",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "MR is active HIGH and asynchronous: a HIGH clears every stage and forces Q0 to Q6 LOW whatever the state of CP. The recovery time trec runs from MR falling to the next HIGH-to-LOW edge on CP."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Clock input",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "CP has Schmitt-trigger action, which makes the counter tolerant of slow rise and fall times on the clock."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Outputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "All seven outputs are fully buffered."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input clamp diodes",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The inputs carry clamp diodes, so with a series current-limiting resistor an input can be driven from a voltage higher than VCC."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Frequency division and time delay circuits."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Standards",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Complies with JEDEC standard no. 7A. Inputs switch at CMOS levels."
  }
 ],
